THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE FETCHED AT RUNTIME (NOT DISTRIBUTED WITH THIS PROJECT)
==========================================================================

make-magic's game-simulation feature drives two third-party programs. Neither is
bundled, vendored, linked, or redistributed by this project. make-magic is a
separate program that invokes MTG Forge as a subprocess (an arms-length
relationship); it downloads both artifacts, on the user's own machine, on first
use, directly from their official upstreams, checksum-verified, and caches them:

  * MTG Forge — the open-source rules engine that runs the AI-vs-AI games.
      License:  GNU General Public License (GPL). See the Card-Forge project.
      Upstream: https://github.com/Card-Forge/forge
      How used: make-magic fetches a pinned Forge release tarball at runtime
                (SHA256-verified) and launches it as a headless `sim` subprocess.
                make-magic does NOT include or redistribute any Forge code,
                binaries, or card data. The GPL of Forge governs the fetched
                Forge artifacts, not make-magic itself, because the two are
                separate programs communicating at arm's length (a subprocess
                invocation), not a combined or derivative work.

  * Eclipse Temurin / OpenJDK (JRE) — the Java runtime Forge requires.
      License:  GPL v2 with the Classpath Exception.
      Upstream: https://adoptium.net (Adoptium API)
      How used: make-magic fetches a Temurin JRE at runtime if no suitable Java
                is already present, and reuses a system Java when available.
                make-magic does NOT redistribute the JRE.

If you already have a compatible Forge install and/or Java, point make-magic at
them with the MAKE_MAGIC_FORGE_HOME and MAKE_MAGIC_JAVA environment variables and
no download occurs. See plugins/make-magic/README.md.

